# Nexus Commerce — Frontend Environment Variables (Production Template)

# Base URL for the backend API endpoint.
#
# Leave this relative for local development. A relative path resolves against
# the origin serving the page, so the same value works on localhost, on a
# phone over a forwarded port, and inside a container; Vite's `/api` proxy
# hands the request to the backend. An absolute http://localhost:... URL
# breaks every client that is not the machine running the server.
#
# Set an absolute URL ONLY for a production build whose API lives on another
# origin, e.g. VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com/api
VITE_API_URL=/api
VITE_APP_NAME="Nexus Commerce"
VITE_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_REPLACE_ME
VITE_FLUTTERWAVE_PUBLIC_KEY=FLWPUBK_TEST-REPLACE_ME
